# genx help prints the usage and succeeds.
exec genx help
stdout '^genx runs an app''s code generation'
! stderr .

# An unknown command is a usage error, exit code 2.
! exec genx frobnicate
stderr '^genx: unknown command "frobnicate"$'

# The temporary module is in place for later scripts.
exists go.mod
grep '^module example.com/app$' go.mod

# Arguments where a command takes none are a usage error too.
! exec genx check extra
cmp stderr want/args.txt

-- want/args.txt --
genx check: takes no arguments

genx runs an app's code generation: producers, then trivial generators.

Usage:

	genx          run every step, write what changed, delete what nothing produces
	genx check    write nothing; fail if any output is stale, missing or left over
	genx list     show the steps in order, and what each reads and writes
	genx help     show this text
